title: SAP ASE (Sybase): Instance
agents: linux
catalog: app/sybase
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors an SAP ASE (Sybase) instance: whether the agent plug-in
 {check_sybase} can connect via {isql} and whether the {dataserver} and
 {backupserver} processes of the instance's OS user are running.

 The states for a failed connection and for missing processes can be
 configured via the rule "SAP ASE (Sybase) Instance" (default: CRIT).

 To use this check, install the agent plug-in {check_sybase} on the host and
 configure the instance in {/etc/check_mk/check_sybase.cfg}.

item:
 The SID of the ASE instance.

discovery:
 One service is created for each instance configured in the agent plug-in.
